<h1>Delete your Atlasphere account</h1>
<p class="info-updated">Last updated: <%= updated %></p>

<p>You can delete your Atlasphere account and its data at any time, from the app, the website, or by email.</p>

<h2>In the app</h2>
<p>Open the <strong>Profile</strong> tab, scroll down and tap <strong>Delete account</strong>, then confirm.</p>

<h2>On the website</h2>
<p>Sign in, go to <a href="/settings">Settings</a> and choose <strong>Delete Account</strong>.</p>

<h2>By email</h2>
<p>If you can’t sign in, email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>?subject=Delete%20my%20Atlasphere%20account"><%= supportEmail %></a> from the address you signed up with and ask us to delete your account. We’ll do it within 30 days and confirm by email.</p>

<h2>What’s deleted</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Your account details (name, email, phone number, gender, password).</li>
  <li>Your profile photo and the places you marked as visited.</li>
  <li>Your friendships and friend requests, and your phone’s push notification registration.</li>
</ul>
<p>Messages you sent in trip chats stay in those chats, so the conversation still makes sense for the others on the trip; ask us by email and we’ll remove them too. Trips you created stay for the other people in them. Copies in our backups are removed as the backups expire, within 30 days.</p>
<p>More detail is in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
